AGPL section 13 -- network use disclosure
================================================================================

If you offer a modified version of rmorie to users over a network (a web
service, a remote API, a SaaS deployment, etc.), section 13 of the AGPL
requires you to make the complete corresponding source code available to
those users. The canonical upstream source is at:

    https://github.com/rootcoder007/rmorie

Modified deployments should either:

  (a) link to the upstream source AND publish their own modifications, or
  (b) operate the service exclusively for users who can already access
      the source (e.g., internal corporate use behind a firewall is OK
      as long as employees can pull the code).

See https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html for the canonical license
text, and https://www.gnu.org/licenses/why-affero-gpl.html for the
project's reasoning behind choosing AGPL over GPL.

